course: dictionary
lesson: 13958
title: Light and happy words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lighthearted describes someone who feels cheerful and free from worry. «The lighthearted puppy chased its tail across the garden.» Nothing is weighing the puppy down, so it is happy and carefree.
explain: Lighthearted can also describe something that is not serious and is meant to be fun. «We watched a lighthearted film about a talking dog.» The film is there to make you laugh, not to make you think about hard problems.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Cheerful, fun, silly and laughed all point to a happy meaning. Heavy, serious or worried would point the other way. Swap in a simple word like happy or fun and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Lighthearted means cheerful and free from worry.
fact: Lighthearted can also mean not serious and meant to be fun, as in «a lighthearted film».
fact: Lighthearted can be written as one word or with a hyphen: lighthearted or light-hearted. Both are correct.
fact: Lighthearted is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a person, a mood or a film.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the Mole runs off lighthearted on a spring day.
exercise: «The lighthearted puppy chased its tail across the garden.» What does lighthearted mean here? | Tired and hungry | *Cheerful and free from worry | Very quiet and still | Angry with its owner
exercise: «We watched a lighthearted film about a talking dog.» What kind of film is it? | Scary and dangerous | Very sad and serious | *Not serious and meant to be fun | Long and boring
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you the quiz is for fun: «The lighthearted quiz was just for fun.» | *lighthearted | fun | just | quiz
test: Maya felt lighthearted after she finished her tests. What does lighthearted mean? | Cold and wet | Very angry | Lost and confused | *Cheerful and free from worry
test: «The clowns told silly jokes all afternoon.» Which clue shows the show is lighthearted? | heavy rain | *silly jokes | cold silence | a sad goodbye
exam: Which word means the opposite of lighthearted? | Joyful | Cheerful | Silly | *Heavy-hearted
